NAME
    dianash - standalone DianaSh command shell

SYNOPSIS
    dianash
    dianash -c <line>...

DESCRIPTION
    Standalone executable for the DianaSh shell, running without an
    attached emulator core. It includes the shell language, builtins,
    sessions, accounts, the sandbox rooted at EmuSen's home directory,
    shipped programs (such as nano(1)), and the linked modules
    dianash.text, emusen.dev, and emusen.testing.

    With no arguments, dianash starts in EmuSen's home directory
    (creating it if needed) and enters an interactive read-eval loop
    with prompt 'DianaSh #: ' (showing the session name once multiple
    sessions exist via tmux(1)) and secondary prompt '> ' for incomplete
    blocks, quotes, or command substitutions.

    Interactive line editing supports Left, Right, Home, and End to move
    the cursor; Up and Down to walk history; Backspace and Delete to
    remove characters; Escape to clear the line; Ctrl-C to cancel the
    current line or interrupt a running command (printing '^C' and
    setting $? to 130); and Ctrl-D on an empty line to exit. When
    standard input is not a terminal, lines are read without echoing.

    Manual pages are loaded from the dianash/man directory beside the
    executable.

OPTIONS
    -c <line>...
        Execute each <line> argument in order as if typed at the prompt,
        then exit with the final line's $? status.

EXAMPLES
    dianash
    dianash -c 'echo hello | cat'
    dianash -c 'for i in 1 2 3; do echo $i; done' 'echo $?'

EXIT STATUS
    0   Interactive shell exited cleanly, or the final -c line succeeded.
    2   Invalid command-line options.
    N   In -c mode, the exit status ($?) of the last executed line.

SEE ALSO
    help(1), man(1), hier(7), modules(7), tmux(1), nano(1)
